  "code": "Blood CS",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Blood Culture</div></td><td><div><br></div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Positive</div></td><td><div>Bacteria or fungi are detected in the blood, indicating a bloodstream infection (bacteremia or fungemia). Further identification of the specific pathogen is necessary for appropriate treatment.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Negative</div></td><td><div>No bacteria or fungi are detected in the blood culture, suggesting no bloodstream infection. However, it does not rule out the possibility of localized infection elsewhere in the body.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Sensitivity Test</div></td><td><div><br></div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Susceptible</div></td><td><div>The pathogen is susceptible to specific antibiotics or antifungal agents tested. These antibiotics or antifungals are likely to be effective in treating the infection.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Resistant</div></td><td><div>The pathogen is resistant to specific antibiotics or antifungal agents tested. These antibiotics or antifungals are unlikely to be effective in treating the infection.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Intermediate</div></td><td><div>The pathogen shows intermediate sensitivity to specific antibiotics or antifungals. The use of these antibiotics or antifungals may still be effective, depending on other factors such as the patient's immune status.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
